1
00:00:00,150 --> 00:00:02,858
It looks like a frozen waterfall.

2
00:00:03,138 --> 00:00:08,204
But the water here is warm… and the white is solid stone.

3
00:00:08,654 --> 00:00:12,479
This is Pamukkale, in western Türkiye.

4
00:00:12,759 --> 00:00:15,280
Its name means "cotton castle."

5
00:00:15,730 --> 00:00:21,640
Seventeen hot springs rise here, full of dissolved calcium carbonate.

6
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:26,027
When the water meets the air, the mineral is left behind

7
00:00:26,307 --> 00:00:28,578
and hardens into travertine.

8
00:00:29,028 --> 00:00:32,715
Layer by layer, it has built white terraces

9
00:00:32,995 --> 00:00:36,339
about two thousand seven hundred metres long.

10
00:00:36,789 --> 00:00:43,570
On top sits Hierapolis, an ancient spa city more than two thousand years old.

11
00:00:43,850 --> 00:00:48,096
Today you can swim among its sunken marble columns.

12
00:00:48,546 --> 00:00:52,890
Since 1988, it has been a UNESCO World Heritage Site.

13
00:00:53,170 --> 00:00:58,728
Would you dare to walk on a castle made of stone that looks like cotton?
